# `geo.store`

Keeping shapes in files.

## Contents

- [`StoreError`](#StoreError): Why a stored shape could not be read back.
- [`Store`](#Store): Where the shapes are kept: the file system stays private.
- [`load`](#load): Reads the text of a stored shape through any file system.

<a id="StoreError"></a>
## `StoreError`

```sisu
pub error StoreError
    Empty
```

Why a stored shape could not be read back.

<a id="Store"></a>
## `Store`

```sisu
pub struct Store
    pub root: Path
    # private fields
```

Where the shapes are kept: the file system stays private.

<a id="Store.new"></a>
### `Store.new`

```sisu
pub def new(fs: Fs, own root: Path) -> Store
```

A store under `root`.

Capabilities: `fs` (`Fs`).

<a id="Store.save"></a>
### `Store.save`

```sisu
pub def save(self, name: Path, s: Shape) -> ! IoError
```

Writes a shape's area to `name`.

Capabilities: `self` (`Fs`).

<a id="load"></a>
## `load`

```sisu
pub def load[F: FsOps](fs: F, path: Path) -> String ! {IoError, StoreError}  # inferred
```

Reads the text of a stored shape through any file system.

Capabilities: `fs` (`Fs`).
